{"book":{"id":"book-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol","slug":"violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol","title":"Violence as a Generative Force: Identity, Nationalism, and Memory in a Balkan Community","authors":[{"id":"person-max-bergholz","name":"Max Bergholz"}],"isbn13":["9781501705885"],"subjects":["Politics & Government"],"topics":["Immigration, Refugees & Borderlands","Crime, Policing & Violence","Death, Memory & Commemoration","Food, Agriculture & Land"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Violence%20as%20a%20Generative%20Force%3A%20Identity%2C%20Nationalism%2C%20and%20Memory%20in%20a%20Balkan%20Community%20Max%20Bergholz","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Violence%20as%20a%20Generative%20Force%3A%20Identity%2C%20Nationalism%2C%20and%20Memory%20in%20a%20Balkan%20Community%20Max%20Bergholz","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Violence%20as%20a%20Generative%20Force%3A%20Identity%2C%20Nationalism%2C%20and%20Memory%20in%20a%20Balkan%20Community%20Max%20Bergholz","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Violence%20as%20a%20Generative%20Force%3A%20Identity%2C%20Nationalism%2C%20and%20Memory%20in%20a%20Balkan%20Community%20Max%20Bergholz","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL21136942W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-laura-shannon-european-studies-laura-shannon-prize-2019-official-winner-page","source-open-library-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol","source-cover-open-library-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol","source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"],"publicationYear":2016,"thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.384,"accessibilityScore":0.082,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"narrative","score":0.68,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"story of\"","catalog text contains \"tells the story\"","catalog text contains \"quest\""]},{"id":"character_driven","score":0.22,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"lives of\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Kulen Vakuf","confidence":0.84}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Local killing in Kulen Vakuf created new perceptions of ethnicity, reshaped community power and nationalism, contradicting the view that nationalism primarily leads to violence.","confidence":0.66},"academicOrientation":{"score":66,"confidence":0.46},"profileConfidence":0.78,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralPlaces":[{"name":"northwest Bosnia and Croatia","confidence":0.42}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"682e16fb4fabc97889cb1c050010b1c779b58aa3ab4557a4d61ea01faa9935fd","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"summary":"During two terrifying days and nights in early September 1941, the lives of nearly two thousand men, women, and children were taken savagely by their neighbors in Kulen Vakuf, a small rural community straddling today’s border between northwest Bosnia and Croatia. This frenzy―in which victims were butchered with farm tools, drowned in rivers, and thrown into deep vertical caves―was the culmination of a chain of local massacres that began earlier in the summer. In Violence as a Generative Force, Max Bergholz tells the story of the sudden and perplexing descent of this once peaceful multiethnic community into extreme violence. This deeply researched microhistory provides provocative insights to questions of global significance: What causes intercommunal violence? How does such violence between neighbors affect their identities and relations? Contrary to a widely held view that sees nationalism leading to violence, Bergholz reveals how the upheavals wrought by local killing actually created dramatically new perceptions of ethnicity―of oneself, supposed \"brothers,\" and those perceived as \"others.\" As a consequence, the violence forged new communities, new forms and configurations of power, and new practices of nationalism.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Massacres","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Ethnic conflict","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Violence","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Nationalism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Memory","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Communalism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-a-balkan-community-max-berghol"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"World war, 1939-1945","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-violence-as-a-generative-force-identity-nationalism-and-memory-in-